<title>UK: Newman Tonks soars on Ingersoll bid.</title>
<headline>Newman Tonks soars on Ingersoll bid.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Newman Tonks Group Plc, in the midst of fighting off a hostile bid from FKI Plc, sharlply extended recent gains in pre-market dealings on Monday as a new suitor entered the frame, dealers said. Ingersoll-Rand Co of the U.S. said it was making a recommended cash offer for Newman, valuing the company at about 230 million stg, a 28.1 percent premium over FKI's bid of 195.7 million stg launched in December  nL27240654.</p>
<p>The shares were indicated 27p higher at 178-1/2p by 0822 GMT.  </p>
<p>Shares in Newman have surged by some 48 percent since mid-December, when the UK building supplier was first approached by FKI, a UK engineering group.</p>
<p>FKI said this morning it had received acceptances for 20.45</p>
<p>--London newsroom +44 171 542 4026</p>
